<p>A rush-hour tram derailed in central Milan on Friday and slammed into a building, killing two people and injuring dozens, police and local officials said. Authorities have opened an investigation into why the tram left the rails. Early reports said the cause was still unclear. Emergency crews treated people at the scene and took the injured to hospital as officials worked to understand the full impact.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/JkdY808AUzjUrCDPyCDdq4VgK4L49wTB95RbJ8xDygZzuOG3rkuEh1iZ9lkvRNzAVDll6vlXuii0uP6lQRasspQkDX0LrIayy3azWErLs3a0-tnNvEwdjI2t7A4P9xPWFr9oIlXXC_Q3qxXv3kZoJn_6aNUKMQiQmtJUZO4jj4bo0OyvlaeKD8qVpKXPBOqjQ2jg5xnzY6qCznucI8W-jDpubfdKyaPYQWrC5hFDwaXpAGaao4Zkz-0oVw' alt='Emergency services work at the scene following a deadly tram derailment in Milan, Italy, February 27, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Where it happened: Le Monde said the crash occurred around 4pm on Vittorio Veneto Street in Milan.</li><li>Vehicle details: Euronews identified the derailed vehicle as a line 9 tram in Milan.</li><li>On-scene account: BBC said the tram was crowded when it crashed.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Mayor Giuseppe Sala: Sala told reporters that one person died after being hit as the tram derailed, and the second victim was a passenger. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/27/tram-derails-and-crashes-into-building-in-milan'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Police: Police said at least 38 people were injured in the crash. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/milan-2-killed-dozens-injured-after-tram-derails-smashes-into-building-in-italy-11147887#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Witnesses: Witnesses at the scene told media the tram was travelling fast. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/tram-derails-in-central-milan-at-least-one-dead'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/milan-2-killed-dozens-injured-after-tram-derails-smashes-into-buil